# NewPostsPill — "Show 12 new posts", the bar that appears at the top of a feed
# when the world moved while you were reading it.
#
# It exists because of what the live stream does WITHOUT it. Posts arrive over
# SSE and the feed re-renders, so a row you were halfway through reading slides
# down the page under your eyes. That is correct data and a broken experience,
# and every product with a live feed has arrived at the same answer: hold the new
# rows back, count them, and let the reader decide when to take them.
#
# ── THE COUNT IS A QUERY, NOT A COUNTER ─────────────────────────────────────
#
# The caller passes `count(t in Post where t.created > seenAt)` — the number of
# rows newer than the marker this reader last caught up to. `seenAt` is an
# ordinary `@client int` cell, and `catchUp` sets it to `now()`.
#
# That shape matters: the number is derived from the data, so it is right after a
# reconnect, right in a second tab, and right when a post is deleted. A
# hand-incremented counter fed by the stream would be none of those, and would
# drift permanently the first time a frame was missed.
#
#     state seenAt: int = 0 @client
#     action catchUp:
#         set seenAt = now()      # (a @client action; no server round trip)
#
#     use NewPostsPill(count(t in Post where t.created > seenAt), catchUp)
#     for t in Post where t.created <= seenAt by created desc limit 50:
#         use PostCard(…)
#
# The feed's own `where` is what actually holds the rows back. This facet only
# reports and invites — it has no way to hide a row, and should not: a component
# that silently filtered a list the caller wrote would be the worst kind of
# surprise.
#
# `a: action` and not a slot, because catching up takes no arguments — which is
# exactly the case an action reference can carry (forms/form.fct explains the
# case it cannot).
app FacetLive:
    css:
        # Sticky rather than fixed: it belongs to the top of the FEED, not to the
        # top of the window, so it stops where the column stops.
        [data-fa-mount] .x-newposts { position: sticky; top: 8px; z-index: 20;
                       display: flex; justify-content: center; padding: 8px 0; }
        [data-fa-mount] .x-newposts button { background: var(--fa-accent); color: #fff; font-weight: 700;
                              font-size: 14px; padding: 8px 16px; border-radius: 9999px;
                              border: none; box-shadow: 0 2px 12px rgba(0,0,0,.35); cursor: pointer; }
        [data-fa-mount] .x-newposts button:hover { filter: brightness(1.08); }
    component NewPostsPill(count: int, a: action):
        if count > 0:
            row class "x-newposts":
                button "Show {count} new posts" -> a
